See @{"Image Provider Settings" link imageprofiles}.

@{b}Speech@{ub}

  @{b}Enabled@{ub}                                toggle
  @{b}Speech Provider Settings...@{ub}             speech system, voice and options

See @{"Speech Provider Settings" link speechprofiles}.

@{b}ARexx@{ub}

  @{b}ARexx Shell@{ub}                            trace mode and a debugging Shell
  @{b}Import Script...@{ub}                       add a script to this menu
  @{b}Run Script@{ub}                             run a script

See @{"ARexx Integration" link arexx}.

@{b}Help@{ub}

  @{b}Open Documentation...@{ub}                  opens this guide
@endnode

@node files "Files and Drawers"
@{b}Files and Drawers@{ub}

Everything AmigaGPT keeps lives under the @{b}AMIGAGPT:@{ub} assign, which the installer adds to S:User-Startup and which points at the drawer you installed into.

@{b}Programs@{ub}

  AMIGAGPT:AmigaGPT           the application
  AMIGAGPT:AmigaGPTD          the daemon
  C:askgpt                    the Shell command, if you installed it

@{b}Your data@{ub}

  AMIGAGPT:config.json        all settings, profiles and API keys
  AMIGAGPT:config.bak         the previous configuration
  AMIGAGPT:chat-history.json  every conversation
  AMIGAGPT:image-history.json every generated image
  AMIGAGPT:images/            the generated image files themselves

If a history file is ever found to be corrupt, AmigaGPT renames it with a .bak extension - or copies it to RAM: if it cannot - tells you what happened, and carries on with an empty history rather than refusing to start.

@{b}Support files@{ub}

  AMIGAGPT:AmigaGPT.guide     this guide, opened by the Help menu
  AMIGAGPT:magic.mgc          the file type database
  AMIGAGPT:rexx/              the bundled ARexx scripts
  AMIGAGPT:devs/speech/34/    where narrator.device v34 goes
  AMIGAGPT:devs/speech/37/    where narrator.device v37 goes
  LOCALE:Catalogs/...         the translations, one drawer per language

magic.mgc may also live in PROGDIR: or C:; see @{"How the file type is worked out" link filetypes}. The scripts in AMIGAGPT:rexx are described in @{"The scripts that are bundled" link arexxbundled}.

@{b}Temporary files@{ub}

  T:AmigaGPTD_history.json    the daemon conversation, until the next reboot
  T:amigagpt_stdout.tmp       Shell Tool output, while a command runs
  T:amigagpt_stderr.tmp       Shell Tool errors, while a command runs

@{b}Backing up@{ub}

Copying AMIGAGPT:config.json, AMIGAGPT:chat-history.json, AMIGAGPT:image-history.json and AMIGAGPT:images/ preserves everything personal. Remember that config.json holds your API keys in plain text.
@endnode

@node language "Language and Catalogs"
@{b}Language and Catalogs@{ub}

AmigaGPT follows the language set in your system Locale preferences. English is built into the program; every other language is provided by a catalog installed into LOCALE:Catalogs.

@{b}Available translations@{ub}

  Bosnian     Croatian            Czech       Danish
  Dutch       English (British)   Finnish     French
  German      Greek               Hungarian   Italian
  Norwegian   Polish              Portuguese  Russian
  Serbian     Slovak              Slovenian   Spanish
  Swedish     Turkish

The installer preselects the language your system is set to, and you can install as many others as you like. To change language afterwards, change it in Locale preferences; if no catalog is installed for the new language, AmigaGPT falls back to English.

To add a language that is missing, or to correct a translation, please open an issue or a pull request. See @{"Contributing" link contributing}.

@{b}Language of the answers@{ub}

The interface language and the language the AI answers in are separate things. To make the model reply in a particular language, put an instruction such as "Always answer in Italian" into the @{b}Chat System@{ub} field of the chat profile. See @{"Chatting" link chatting}.
@endnode

@node troubleshooting "Troubleshooting"
@{b}Troubleshooting@{ub}

@{b}"Could not open muimaster.library"@{ub}
MUI is not installed, or is older than version 3. Install MUI and reboot. See @{"System Requirements" link requirements}.

@{b}"Could not find all the MUI custom classes"@{ub}
One of MCC_NList, MCC_TextEditor or MCC_Guigfx is missing. Install all three and reboot.

@{b}"Could not open codesets.library"@{ub}
Install codesets.library 6.22 or higher.

@{b}The app crashes randomly when started from the Shell@{ub}
The stack is too small. Run STACK 32768 before starting AmigaGPT. See @{"Launching AmigaGPT" link launching}.

@{b}"Please enter your API key"@{ub}
The selected profile has no key. See @{"Entering your API key" link apikey}.

@{b}"Error connecting. Please try again."@{ub}
Your TCP/IP stack is not online, or the host and port in the profile are wrong, or AmiSSL is missing or too old for an SSL connection. Check that you can reach the internet, then use @{b}Test@{ub} in the provider settings window to see the exact response from the server.

@{b}"Invalid request"@{ub}
Usually a provider account with no credit left, or a model your account is not entitled to use. Check your balance with the provider and try a smaller model.

@{b}The reply appears all at once instead of streaming@{ub}
The server does not support streaming, or @{b}Streaming@{ub} is off for that profile. See @{"Chat Provider Settings" link chatprofiles}.

@{b}Speech does nothing, or reports a missing component@{ub}
Cloud voices need AHI. narrator.device v34 and v37 need both the device file and translator.library v42 or higher. Flite needs flite.device. See @{"Speech Provider Settings" link speechprofiles} and @{"Installation" link installation}.

@{b}Generated images do not display@{ub}
Install a PNG datatype, and MCC_Guigfx together with render.library and guigfx.library.

@{b}An attachment is sent as the wrong type@{ub}
magic.mgc is not where AmigaGPT can find it, so the type is being guessed from the file name. See @{"How the file type is worked out" link filetypes}.

@{b}ARexx commands do nothing@{ub}
Check which port you are addressing - AMIGAGPT for the application, AMIGAGPTD for the daemon. On MorphOS you also need the 68k version of ARexx installed. See @{"ARexx Integration" link arexx}.

@{b}"Could not open documentation"@{ub}
This guide is not at AMIGAGPT:AmigaGPT.guide. Copy it into the AmigaGPT drawer.

@{b}Everything looks wrong after changing settings@{ub}
@{b}Clear MUI Settings@{ub} in the @{b}View@{ub} menu resets the whole interface to its defaults.

@{b}Reporting a problem@{ub}

Please open an issue at https://github.com/sacredbanana/AmigaGPT with your machine, operating system version, AmigaGPT version and what you were doing at the time.
@endnode

@node developing "Developing"
@{b}Developing@{ub}

Source code is hosted at https://github.com/sacredbanana/AmigaGPT

You can compile the code natively or with Docker.

@{b}Native@{ub}

@{i}Building the AmigaOS 3 app@{ui}

You need Bebbo's @{b}amiga-gcc@{ub} toolchain from https://github.com/bebbo/amiga-gcc

Once it is installed, download the additional SDKs (AmiSSL, Translator, json-c) from https://github.com/sacredbanana/AmigaSDK-gcc and put them into the Amiga development environment you installed above.

@{i}Building the AmigaOS 4 app@{ui}

Set up the toolchain from https://github.com/sba1/adtools

Once it is installed, get the same SDKs from https://github.com/sacredbanana/AmigaSDK-gcc and put them into that development environment.

@{b}Docker@{ub}

An all-in-one Docker image can build all three versions of the app.

Install Docker and run build_os3.sh, build_os4.sh or build_morphos.sh depending on which version you want. Set CLEAN=1 for a clean build, for example CLEAN=1 ./build_os3.sh, and DEBUG=1 for a debug build.

The built programs are written to the out directory. package.sh performs a clean build of all three, copies the executables and the compiled catalogs into the bundle, and produces the distribution archive.

@{b}Translations@{ub}

Interface strings are gettext catalogs. The template is catalogs/AmigaGPT.pot and each language has its own .po file under catalogs. The build regenerates the catalog sources and compiles a .catalog for each language.
@endnode

@node contributing "Contributing"
@{b}Contributing to AmigaGPT@{ub}

Contributions to AmigaGPT are welcome. If you have a bug to report, a feature to suggest, a translation to add or improve, or a change you would like to make to the code, please open an issue or submit a pull request at https://github.com/sacredbanana/AmigaGPT
@endnode

